    "status": "on_track",
    "notes": "The back strength index rose from 106 to 110 this period, which is a meaningful and encouraging gain and the clearest sign of progressive overload working as intended. Biceps held steady at 104, chest at 100, and shoulders at 101 — all flat, suggesting no overload was applied to those muscle groups this period, though they are not priorities given your goal. Legs also remained unchanged at 103. Overall, overload is on track where it matters most: the back."
